{"author":{"id":"8d2e0405f08ac6c481f912544d6d5c0f58b2dc14a7e51ad4d499ee7a34567943"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1795701170,"nonce":"lpm1Gk28VE7V+ak+6VGDoSFe8ok=","title":"Seven cuDSS tests fail on GPU on main: complex solves with a parameter, and a pattern-size mismatch","message":"On a GPU run of main (`JAX_PLATFORMS=cuda,cpu`, cuDSS 0.8 and nvmath-python installed) the two cuDSS test files fail 7 of 8 tests. They pass on the host backend.\n\n**What goes wrong.** Two distinct errors:\n\n1. `NotImplementedError: fem.solve(\u003ccomplex-native linear or precond\u003e, \u003cparameter\u003e=...): the complex-native solve works on the assembled Re/Im legs, which carry no runtime parameter, so the values would be dropped. Use a real-equivalent solver (e.g. jno.solve.lu(backend='host')), or build the form with the value fixed.` Seen in tests/test_solve_cudss_ldl.py::test_solution_matches_host_lu (a complex form solved with `lu(backend=\"cudss\")` and a runtime `k=` array) and in tests/test_cudss_release.py::test_an_eager_solve_frees_its_factors. The tests pass a runtime parameter to a complex solve through cuDSS; the library now refuses that combination.\n2. `RuntimeError` at jno/utils/solver/linear.py ~913: \"jno.solve.lu(backend='cudss'): the operator's pattern has 9820 entries under this trace and 19640 in the FEM's compiled pattern; refusing to factor values against the wrong pattern.\" The traced operator has exactly half the entries of the compiled pattern, which looks like the complex operator traced as one real block while the compiled pattern is the doubled real-equivalent (Re/Im) pattern.\n\nThe failing tests: tests/test_cudss_release.py (3: `test_release_frees_the_extra_slots_and_they_still_work`, `test_core_releases_between_programs`, `test_an_eager_solve_frees_its_factors`) and tests/test_solve_cudss_ldl.py (4: `test_solution_matches_host_lu`, `test_jit_gradient_matches_host_lu_and_two_solves_per_program`, `test_values_that_are_not_symmetric`, `test_integrate_with_the_cudss_solver_takes_the_ldl_path`). I looked closely at two of them; which of the two errors each of the others raises I did not separate (the run printed only the last of them).\n\n**Reproduce.** On a GPU: `JAX_PLATFORMS=cuda,cpu XLA_PYTHON_CLIENT_PREALLOCATE=false pytest tests/test_cudss_release.py tests/test_solve_cudss_ldl.py` (7 failed, 1 passed, about 20 s).\n\n**Expected.** The cuDSS complex path (symmetric LDL, differentiable) solves a complex form with a runtime parameter, as these tests assert and as the host backend does, or the tests are updated to say it is unsupported and the refusal gives a path that works on cuDSS.\n\n**Where.** jno/_fem.py (the complex-native refusal, near the complex solve path); jno/utils/solver/linear.py (~913, the pattern check for the complex LDL path); jno/utils/solver/cudss_sym.py.\n\n**Workaround.** `lu(backend=\"host\")`, or a real-equivalent form.\n\n**Direction.** First split the seven by error. The pattern mismatch is probably one size bookkeeping bug (complex versus real-equivalent pattern) and may account for all of the second group; the first error needs a decision whether runtime parameters are supported on this path.","files":null}]}